discussion_comments.comment_body:
It looks like his issue was https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/issues/138826 which was fixed in https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/pull/139251. Those signals conflicted with C++ macros from signal.h so they were prefixed to resolve the conflict.

Our issue is a little different, since that was a macro conflict and ours is the proto scoping rule. Prefixing still seems like the better choice, so we could have something like:

```proto
enum CgroupMountMode {
	CGROUP_MOUNT_MODE_READ_ONLY = 0;
	CGROUP_MOUNT_MODE_WRITABLE = 1;

	... or this if we want to shorten ...

	CGROUP_READ_ONLY = 0;
	CGROUP_WRITABLE = 1;
}
```

